From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Trade items made while playing (enchanted gear, potions, scrolls)

- items.lua describes a generated item as plain data, gives it a key both sides compute, and rebuilds it (validated and
  clamped; unknown effects, missing models and unknown kinds are refused; no scripts)
- the trade window offers generated items by key and sends their descriptions; MpTradeExec finds ours by key and
  rebuilds theirs
- items_test.lua covers key stability over JSON, rebuilding and refusal of bad data

---
